## Users live in memory, so create user 1 first (see auth.endpoint.http)

## Create draft (publishedAt: null) - expect 201
POST http://localhost:3000/posts
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "authorId": 1,
    "title": "My First Post!",
    "content": "A post long enough to pass the thirty character minimum."
}

###
## Create and publish - expect 201, slug "my-first-post-2" if the title is taken
POST http://localhost:3000/posts
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "authorId": 1,
    "title": "My First Post!",
    "content": "A post long enough to pass the thirty character minimum.",
    "publish": true
}

###
## Unknown author - expect 404
POST http://localhost:3000/posts
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "authorId": 999,
    "title": "My First Post!",
    "content": "A post long enough to pass the thirty character minimum."
}

###
## Missing title (@IsNotEmpty) - expect 400
POST http://localhost:3000/posts
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "authorId": 1,
    "content": "A post long enough to pass the thirty character minimum."
}

###
## content too short, under 30 chars (@MinLength(30)) - expect 400
POST http://localhost:3000/posts
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "authorId": 1,
    "title": "My First Post!",
    "content": "Too short"
}

###
## publish as string (@IsBoolean) - expect 400
POST http://localhost:3000/posts
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "authorId": 1,
    "title": "My First Post!",
    "content": "A post long enough to pass the thirty character minimum.",
    "publish": "yes"
}

###
## Server-owned fields (forbidNonWhitelisted) - expect 400
POST http://localhost:3000/posts
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "authorId": 1,
    "title": "My First Post!",
    "content": "A post long enough to pass the thirty character minimum.",
    "slug": "custom",
    "publishedAt": "2020-01-01T00:00:00.000Z"
}

###
## Empty body, every required field missing - expect 400
POST http://localhost:3000/posts
Content-Type: application/json

{}
